            <div xml:id="d914">

                <pb facs="1200" n="1076" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg1076"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.672/92</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Special Mission at
                            Lausanne to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lausanne</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-06-02"><hi rendition="#italic">June 2,
                        1923</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received June 21.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 30–A</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith one
                    copy of the long form of treaty prepared by Mr. Hackworth and Mr. Turlington, as
                    well as one copy of the short form of treaty, as mentioned in my telegram No.
                    393, June 2, 1 a.m.</p>
                <p>One copy of each of these two forms is also being sent to the Embassy in Paris in
                    case the Department desires the text transmitted by wire to Washington.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Mission:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">F. L.
                        Belin</hi></signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Secretary
                    General</hi></closer>



                <xi:include href="d914-a1.xml" xpointer="d914-a1"/>
